# Tempo / TraceQL compatibility smoke corpus.
#
# PR 4 lifted-and-adapted the cases from compatibility/prometheus/
# shadow/traceql_shadow_test.go::traceqlInstantCases(). PR 5 extended the
# corpus with /api/metrics/query_range + /api/metrics/query cases and
# added the semantic-consistency layer (see differ.go::SemanticConsistency).
# The three metrics_instant cases activated alongside the cerberus
# /api/metrics/query handler (see internal/api/tempo/metrics_query_instant.go).
#
# 4 cases mined from upstream in #1709 diverged from reference Tempo on
# arrival and were held OUT of this corpus per driver/corpus.go's "no
# opt-out marker, a case that can't run is removed" contract (real
# divergences never enter the baseline). Both filed bugs are now fixed
# and the 4 cases are re-added in their own section below
# ("Trace-scoped root identity + NOT-evaluation parity"):
#   * scoped_trace_root_service, scoped_trace_root_name_regex,
#     scoped_trace_duration_gt — cerberus used to fold trace:rootService /
#     trace:rootName / trace:duration comparisons to constant-false
#     instead of computing real answers; now lowers to a real per-trace
#     correlated subquery (#1711).
#   * negated_kind_not_client — reference Tempo returns empty for any
#     top-level `!(<comparison>)` spanset filter regardless of the
#     inner comparison's selectivity; cerberus now reproduces that
#     bit-for-bit instead of computing the logically-correct
#     (non-empty) answer (#1712).
#
# The shadow test runs the SAME 20 search categories against a fake
# in-process span set; this corpus runs the SAME categories against
# real Tempo + real cerberus, fed by harness/.../driver/seeder.go's
# deterministic OTLP push.
#
# Seeder fixture shape (see seeder.go):
#   * 4 services: checkout, payments, search, shipping
#   * 25 traces per service (100 traces total)
#   * Each trace: 1 root span (Server, "GET /api/<svc>/<idx>", 150ms)
#     + 2-4 children (rotating kinds, every 5th child = ERROR)
#   * Resource attrs: service.name, deployment.env="compat-test",
#     telemetry.sdk="cerberus-tempo-compat-seeder", trace.fixture="pr3"
#   * Span attrs (root): http.method=GET, http.target=/api/<svc>/<idx>,
#     trace.index=<idx>
#   * Span attrs (child): child.index, kind
#   * Status: Ok (default), Error for every 5th child
#   * Anchor: rolling — recomputed per run as `now() - 5m` (see
#     driver/seeder.go::currentAnchor). Each trace shifted by (svcIdx*25 +
#     traceIdx) seconds — last trace lands ~400s after anchor.
#
# Diff strategy reminder (see differ.go top-of-file):
#   * Trace IDs are the diff key as-is: cerberus emits the real
#     hex(TraceId), so byte-equality across backends is the contract and
#     a mismatch surfaces as missing_in_a / missing_in_b rather than
#     being canonicalised away.
#   * Numeric fields compare under 1e-9 relative epsilon.
#   * Cardinality is reported as a reason but every key-level miss is
#     also surfaced under missing_in_a / missing_in_b.
#   * Metrics-endpoint cases canonicalise series by label-set hash; the
#     differ also runs semantic-consistency assertions per backend
#     (avg ≡ sum/count, exemplars belong to their parent series).
#
# Cases below cover the 7 shadow categories (attribute matchers per
# scope (5), intrinsics (4), structural ops (4), set ops (3), inner
# aggregates (2)) plus 7 metrics-pipeline cases (4 range + 3 instant)
# and a per-id smoke; later additions grew the spanSets, metrics, and
# nil-comparison families (the count below tracks
# `grep -c '^-- name --'`).
# Total: 68 cases (`grep -c '^-- name --'`) — 51 from the families
# above (the nil-comparison family activated alongside the Traces
# Drilldown breakdown fix, intrinsic `!= nil` lowering), 4 from the
# trace-scoped root-identity + NOT-evaluation-parity block re-added by
# #1711/#1712, and 12 from the upstream-mined block described next.
# Plus one anchored-regex regression case
# (resource_service_name_regex_prefix_no_overmatch, issue #1741 —
# "check" is a strict prefix of the seeded "checkout" service name,
# never the whole string, so an anchored `=~` must match zero traces
# on both backends; a substring-search lowering would wrongly match
# every checkout trace).
#
# The "Upstream-mined" block at the end of this file (#1522) is a
# different provenance from everything above: every case above was
# written by a cerberus author reasoning about what to test. These are
# lifted from grafana/tempo's OWN pkg/traceql table tests (parse_test.go
# / ast_execute_test.go), ported as query strings only — no upstream
# AST/parser code is vendored or linked (that stays test-only /
# quarantined per docs/upstream-forks.md; the agpl-clean gate enforces
# it). Each case cites the upstream Test function it was mined from.
# Every candidate was validated to (a) parse and (b) lower cleanly via
# internal/traceql before being added — one candidate
# (`{ } | max(duration) - min(duration) >= 0`, mirroring
# TestScalarExpressionOperators/TestArithmetic's scalar-arithmetic
# coverage) failed to lower (`lowerScalarExpr` has no case for
# ast.ScalarOperation) and was left OUT of the corpus rather than added
# red — see #1708, which tracks the fix and re-adding the case once it
# lands.

